lines=['# M4 preparation and live-sanity experiment audit','', '**Overall verdict: WARN. No integrity BLOCK for the narrowly qualified known-target sanity statement below.**','', '**Date:** 2026-09-27 (Asia/Tokyo). **Auditor:** GPT-6-Astra ultra, fresh agent `/root/m4_sanity_audit`. **Assurance:** same-family / provisional. Deterministic arithmetic and record checks passed; semantic acceptance remains provisional.','',warranted,'', '## Scope and method','', 'Read the isolated manifest/environment description, both baseline artifacts, baseline comparison, all three preserved sanity traces, the relevant runner/planner/guard/oracle code, tracker and code-review addenda. No network, Kubernetes, Ansible, API or GPU operation was run, and no implementation/result artifact was changed. Offline pure-function replays use saved probe rows through a mock. **247 deterministic checks pass across 20 windows and 3,000 requests.** Full checks, input hashes and inspected-source snapshots are under `.aris/traces/experiment-audit/20260927_m4_sanity/`.','', '## A. Ground-truth provenance — WARN','',checks['gt_provenance']['details'],'','The runner hardcodes namespace, service and fault, constructs a 0.99-confidence RCA report from its own known injection object, and uses `use_llm=False` (`scripts/e2r/run_recovery_sanity.py:17`, `:214`, `:220`). The value 0.99 is neither learned diagnostic confidence nor measured accuracy. The live object JSON and target-bound precondition make the single cleanup action inspectable; they do not exercise graph diagnosis. The independent HTTP collector supplies the workload measurements, and the baseline is a separate no-fault interval. No evidence of model-output-derived fake ground truth was found.','', '## B. Metric arithmetic and normalization — PASS','', 'For every raw window, all 150 attempts have finite, nonnegative latencies; attempts equal samples and valid-latency count, successes equal 150, and the error rate is zero. Nearest-rank p95 is `sorted(latencies)[ceil(0.95*n)-1]`; throughput is `successes/elapsed_seconds`. No failed requests are removed by the collector’s latency expression; in these artifacts all requests succeeded. Canary outcomes are recorded true, but their HTTP bodies/status records are not retained.','', 'The pooled baseline p95 uses all 900 latency values. Baseline throughput is the median of six window throughputs, not 900 divided by the wall-clock span including five inter-window gaps (`scripts/e2r/run_recovery_baseline.py:118`). This declared aggregation reproduces exactly. Source computation is at historical `workload_oracle.py:155` and `rca_bench/recovery_oracle.py:89`.','', '| Artifact | Window | Requests | p95 ms | Throughput rps | Error rate | Canary |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
